      "writtenOn": "2022-11-14T19:16:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So what makes these calls `unsafe`? The parameters are already validated by the type system; is it about making sure that the C code can be \"trusted\" to not have side effects and/or respect the constness of its received pointers?",
      "parentUuid": "c93a9306_58d7201d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 331,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 331,
        "endChar": 80
      },
