      "message": "Could we avoid `panic`? It\u0027s always cleaner to return an error. I know our panic handler is pretty simple, but abruptly jumping to it can still create inconsistent state that is difficult to argue about. Returning an error means we properly destroy objects before printing the error message.\n\nYou already have a few places where you convert to FdtError::Internal. Maybe we could give it a string with context? Or create a separate enum value for things like this.",
